Package: BINTS
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Hierarchical Spatio-Temporal Models of Insect Biomass and
    Species Richness
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person(
      given = "Kwaku Peprah",
      family = "Adjei",
      email = "kwaku.adjei@nina.no",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: Fits Bayesian hierarchical models of insect biomass and species
    richness, separately or jointly, with NIMBLE. Biomass follows a truncated
    normal distribution with the truncation at zero built into the likelihood
    (a log-normal is available), and richness a truncated normal, Poisson or
    negative binomial distribution. Models combine fixed effects,
    random year, locality and replicate effects, linear or cyclic temporal
    effects, spatial effects (a nearest-neighbour Gaussian process or a
    coordinate spline), and an optional space-time interaction. For joint models
    effects can be shared as parameters, as latent processes with response
    specific loadings, or as correlated response-specific effects. The package
    runs reproducible multi-chain MCMC with recorded seeds, and provides
    prediction, posterior predictive checks, spatial maps and diagnostic plots.
    The earlier 'create_insect_*' functions for building and running NIMBLE
    models, and a helper for cyclic spline bases, are retained.
